Debricking using Serial. In that case a USB to Serial, but it's similar with other Serial connectors to your computer.

Generic pre-requisits: 
  * serial connected from your machine to the router
  * terminal program (e.g. minicom, screen,...) set to **115200**
  * tftp server (e.g. dnsmasq,...)
  * copy a working & full OpenWrt firmware image into your tftp server folder

Steps (USB to Serial example):
  * Connect from router serial to our serial in this way (numbered pins in router):
  - empty (not necessary)
  - RX in router to TX in computer 
  - TX in router to RX in computer
  - GND in both

  * Configure computer
<code>
 sudo ip addr add 10.10.10.3/24 dev 
 sudo dnsmasq -d --port=0 --enable-tftp --tftp-root=/tmp/tftp/firmware/
</code>
  * Connect to router
<code> 
 screen /dev/ttyUSB0 115200
</code>
  * Turn on router (e.g. plug PoE).

